cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "transport-ingest-c: the ingest transport layer, in C over picoquic"
abstract: >
  A transport layer is the input that triggers an interactor. This one terminates the
  client transport, decodes player input datagrams, and hands the result to
  the game interactor over iceoryx2. It carries player traffic, which is why it
  is C and why it links one QUIC implementation and one TLS library rather than
  whichever each end preferred: the Godot client's WebTransportPeer uses the same
  pair, so both ends of a connection are the same code.
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    email: ernest.lee@chibifire.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4570-1436"
version: 0.1.0-dev.1
date-released: "2026-08-17"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric/transport-ingest-c"
keywords:
  - quic
  - webtransport
  - http3
  - multiplayer
  - iceoryx2

# Vendored under thirdparty/, so these are not fetched at build time and the versions
# are this repository's to state. transport-ingest-python is the second implementation
# of the same contract and shares none of this list, which is the point of having it.
references:

  - type: software
    title: "picoquic: a minimal implementation of QUIC"
    authors:
      - family-names: Huitema
        given-names: Christian
    url: "https://github.com/private-octopus/picoquic"
    notes: >
      The QUIC implementation, vendored at thirdparty/picoquic. HTTP/3 and WebTransport
      come from its own picohttp -- h3zero_server.c, h3zero_common.c, webtransport.c.
      This serves no web pages, so it links no HTTP server library.

  - type: software
    title: "picotls: a TLS 1.3 implementation"
    url: "https://github.com/h2o/picotls"
    notes: "Vendored at thirdparty/picotls. The TLS layer picoquic runs over."

  - type: software
    title: "Mbed TLS"
    url: "https://github.com/Mbed-TLS/mbedtls"
    notes: >
      Vendored at thirdparty/mbedtls, reached through picotls. It is the backend the
      Godot client's WebTransportPeer uses, and matching it is why it is here rather
      than whichever backend was easiest.

  - type: software
    title: "picoquic-godot-patches"
    notes: >
      Vendored at thirdparty/picoquic-godot-patches. The diffs that make this picoquic
      and the Godot client's agree; a patch set kept as a directory rather than as a
      fork so what was changed stays legible.

  - type: software
    title: "contract-bus: the weft plane harness"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lee
        given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    url: "https://github.com/v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric/contract-bus"
    notes: >
      Vendored at thirdparty/harness. The iceoryx2 C ABI as a dlsym dispatch table, the
      shared limits, and the payload types. Every plane and edge links it.

  - type: software
    title: "iceoryx2: zero-copy lock-free inter-process communication"
    authors:
      - name: "ekxide IO GmbH"
    url: "https://github.com/eclipse-iceoryx/iceoryx2"
    notes: "The bus the decoded result is handed to an interactor over. Reached through the harness ABI, never linked directly."
